    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **273 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for owners:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to the `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 when creating an owner, if no registration date is present it defaults to `LocalDate.now()` (today) before saving.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `registrationDate` to the `Owner` response schema as a read-only `string`/`format: date` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, and MapStruct maps it automatically by name into the owner response.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) so the mapping works across every persistence profile (ddl-auto is `none`).\n\nThe new acceptance test `Cp08Tests` (asserting `$.registrationDate` equals today) passes, along with all existing tests across the JDBC, JPA, and Spring Data JPA arms.",
